note <a raise is caught on the native backends as on TypeScript, its fields whole, and an uncaught one ends the program>

# Ported from guard-native.ts by statement (item term-self-host-001-0655), one test per `ok` in its order: swift, kotlin,
# rust (note/project/term/hive/11-native-exceptions.md). A program with a guarded call and an unguarded one is compiled
# against the stdlib for each backend, built by the real toolchain and run. The guarded path returns the handler's
# answer with the exception's fields whole. The unguarded raise, reached when the program is given an argument, ends it
# with a non-zero exit and the exception's form and note on stderr. Kotlin also answers a division and a remainder by
# zero with the `defect` TypeScript raises.
#
# The original compiled through a front end of its own (parse, mill, bind, check, simplify over the program's roots).
# Here compile-text compiles it over the stdlib under each env, as withNativeEnv(env, stdlibResolver()) asked, the roots
# its entries. Each leg's main is written in the backend's own words as the original wrote it, and each leg is built
# once, by the first test that asks. A leg whose toolchain is missing skips each of its tests, where the original
# printed one skip line, and a leg that did not build skips the tests after its build test, which fails. GN_ONLY=swift,
# kotlin or rust runs one.

load ../support/compiling
  find compile-text
  find compile-choice
  find compile-outcome
  find emit-text
  find prelude-text

load ../support/running
  find run-tool

load ../support/temp
  find temp-folder

load @term/base/process/run
  find run
  find run-result

load @term/base/process/tool
  find find-tool

load @term/base/environment
  find variable

load @term/base/file
  find write, name write-file

load @term/base/file/directory
  find make, name make-folder

load @term/base/text
  find split, name text-split
  find contains, name text-contains

dock load
  load <@term/make/code/compile/kotlin>, name guard-kotlin
  load <node:os>, name guard-os
  load <node:path>, name guard-path

# a guarded lookup and an unguarded one, over an exception with a prop of its own
host program, <load @term/base/code/exception\n  find absence\n\nform user-absence\n  like absence\n    bind note, \<No such user\>\n    link key, like text\n\ntask find-user\n  take key, like text\n  like text\n  fork test\n    hook test\n      call is-equal\n        read key\n        text \<a\>\n    hook hold\n      send back, text \<alice\>\n    hook miss\n      halt user-absence\n        bind thing, text \<user\>\n        bind key, read key\n\ntask lookup\n  take key, like text\n  like text\n  fork\n    mark unsafe\n    save found\n      call find-user\n        read key\n    send back\n      read found\n  halt take\n    take problem\n    send back\n      text \<caught \{\{problem/form\}\}: \{\{problem/note\}\}\>\n\ntask unguarded\n  take key, like text\n  like text\n  send back\n    call find-user\n      read key\n\ntask describe\n  take key, like text\n  like text\n  fork\n    mark unsafe\n    send back\n      call find-user\n        read key\n  halt take\n    take problem\n    fork case, read problem\n      case user-absence\n        send back, text \<no user \{\{key\}\}: \{\{note\}\}\>\n\n# an INTERPOLATED text raises `failure` like a plain one. It was a `template` node every emitter's throw case\n# missed: Rust handed back a String where the carrier goes (test/compile/halt-text.ts holds TypeScript)\ntask need-key\n  take key, like text\n  like text\n  halt \<no such key \{\{key\}\}\>\n\ntask checked\n  take key, like text\n  like text\n  fork\n    mark unsafe\n    send back\n      call need-key\n        read key\n  halt take\n    take problem\n    send back\n      text \<caught \{\{problem/form\}\}: \{\{problem/note\}\}\>\n\n# a raise from INSIDE an arm that binds the caught exception's `time`. The raise stamps its own time through the\n# stdlib's `exception-time` (`call now`, the clock module), which was inlined into the arm as `time.now()`, where\n# `time` is the caught number on Swift and Kotlin, and the file did not build (2026-10-04)\ntask translate\n  take key, like text\n  like text\n  fork\n    mark unsafe\n    send back\n      call find-user\n        read key\n  halt take\n    take problem\n    fork case, read problem\n      case user-absence\n        fork test\n          hook test\n            call is-above\n              read time\n              code 0\n          hook hold\n            halt absence\n              bind thing, text \<translated \{\{key\}\}\>\n        send back, text \<no time\>\n\ntask translated\n  take key, like text\n  like text\n  fork\n    mark unsafe\n    send back\n      call translate\n        read key\n  halt take\n    take problem\n    fork case, read problem\n      case absence\n        send back, read thing\n      hook miss\n        send back, text \<another exception\>\n\n# a division and a remainder by zero, guarded. TypeScript and Kotlin raise the `defect` the guard catches. Swift traps\n# and Rust panics, which no guard reaches (decisions-2026-10.md D15), so those two build this and do not run it\ntask share\n  take total, like number\n  take parts, like number\n  like text\n  fork\n    mark unsafe\n    save got\n      call divide\n        read total\n        read parts\n    send back, text \<\{got\}\>\n  halt take\n    take problem\n    send back, text \<caught \{problem/form\}\>\n\ntask rest\n  take total, like number\n  take parts, like number\n  like text\n  fork\n    mark unsafe\n    save got\n      call modulo\n        read total\n        read parts\n    send back, text \<\{got\}\>\n  halt take\n    take problem\n    send back, text \<caught \{problem/form\}\>\n>

# the answers every backend must give: the happy path, the caught raise with its fields, the uncaught raise
host want-found, <alice>

host want-caught, <caught user-absence: No such user>

host want-cased, <no user zed: No such user>

host want-text, <caught failure: no such key q>

host want-translated, <translated zed>

# each leg's main, as the original wrote it: the five guarded calls, and the unguarded one when given an argument
host swift-main, <print(lookup(key: "a"))\nprint(lookup(key: "b"))\nprint(describe(key: "zed"))\nprint(checked(key: "q"))\nprint(translated(key: "zed"))\nif CommandLine.arguments.count \> 1 \{ print(try! unguarded(key: "z")) \}\n>

host kotlin-main, <fun main(args: Array\<String\>) \{ println(lookup("a")); println(lookup("b")); println(describe("zed")); println(checked("q")); println(translated("zed")); println(share(6, 3)); println(share(6, 0)); println(rest(7, 0)); if (args.isNotEmpty()) \{ println(unguarded("z")) \} \}\n>

host rust-main, <fn main() \{ println!("\{\}", lookup("a".to_string())); println!("\{\}", lookup("b".to_string())); println!("\{\}", describe("zed".to_string())); println!("\{\}", checked("q".to_string())); println!("\{\}", translated("zed".to_string())); if std::env::args().count() \> 1 \{ match unguarded("z".to_string()) \{ Ok(v) =\> println!("\{\}", v), Err(e) =\> \{ eprintln!("\{\}", e); std::process::exit(1) \} \} \} \}\n>

# the stdlib's exception module docks crates (uuid for the occurrence code, base64 for its tone shape), so the Rust
# leg builds as a cargo package, sharing the roundtrip's target dir so the crates build once per machine
host cargo-toml, <[package]\nname = "term-guard-native"\nversion = "0.1.0"\nedition = "2021"\n\n[dependencies]\nregex = "1"\nsha2 = "0.10"\nmd-5 = "0.10"\nhmac = "0.12"\nbase64 = "0.22"\nhex = "0.4"\nuuid = \{ version = "1", features = ["v4"] \}\nrand = "0.8"\nchrono = "0.4"\nserde_json = "1"\nunicode-normalization = "0.1"\nunicode-segmentation = "1"\n>

# one backend built and run. `state` is <skipped>, <failed> (the compile or the build) or <ran>. `lines` is what the
# program printed run plainly, `raised-code` and `raised-error` its exit and stderr run with an argument
form guard-leg
  link state, like text
  link reason, like text, fall <>
  link lines
    like list, like text
    fall make list
  link raised-code, like number, fall 0
  link raised-error, like text, fall <>

# every leg made in this process, by its backend: a leg is built once, by the first test that asks
form guard-legs
  mark shared
  link held, like hash, like text, like guard-leg

host guard-held, make(guard-legs, bind(held, make hash))

# the program's roots, the original's simplify roots
task roots
  like list, like text

  back make list(<lookup>, <unguarded>, <describe>, <checked>, <translated>, <share>, <rest>)

task compiled
  take env, like text
  like compile-outcome

  back compile-text(program, make(compile-choice, bind(file, <main.tree>), bind(stdlib, env), bind(env, env), bind(entries, roots())))

task leg-skipped
  take reason, like text
  like guard-leg

  back make(guard-leg, bind(state, <skipped>), bind(reason, reason))

task leg-failed
  take reason, like text
  like guard-leg

  back make(guard-leg, bind(state, <failed>), bind(reason, reason))

task leg-ran
  take plain, like run-result
  take raised, like run-result
  like guard-leg

  back make(guard-leg, bind(state, <ran>), bind(lines, text-split(plain/output, <\n>)), bind(raised-code, raised/code), bind(raised-error, raised/error))

task swift-leg
  like guard-leg

  fork test, is-equal(find-tool(<swiftc>), <>)
    hold
      back leg-skipped(<swiftc not installed>)
  save out, compiled(<swift>)
  fork test, not(out/ok)
    hold
      back leg-failed(out/messages/join(< | >))
  save folder, temp-folder(<term-guard-native->)
  save main, guard-path/join(folder, <main.swift>)
  write-file(main, <{prelude-text(out, <swift>)}\n{emit-text(out, <swift>)}\n{swift-main}>)
  save binary, guard-path/join(folder, <swift-main>)
  save failed, run-tool(make list(<swiftc>, <-o>, binary, main))
  fork test, is-unequal(failed, <>)
    hold
      back leg-failed(failed)
  back leg-ran(run(binary, make list), run(binary, make list(<raise>)))

task kotlin-leg
  like guard-leg

  fork test, or(is-equal(find-tool(<kotlinc>), <>), is-equal(find-tool(<java>), <>))
    hold
      back leg-skipped(<kotlinc/java not installed>)
  save out, compiled(<kotlin>)
  fork test, not(out/ok)
    hold
      back leg-failed(out/messages/join(< | >))
  save folder, temp-folder(<term-guard-native->)
  save file, guard-path/join(folder, <main.kt>)
  write-file(file, guard-kotlin/hoist-kotlin-imports(<{prelude-text(out, <kotlin>)}\n{emit-text(out, <kotlin>)}\n{kotlin-main}>))
  save jar, guard-path/join(folder, <main.jar>)
  save failed, run-tool(make list(<kotlinc>, file, <-include-runtime>, <-d>, jar))
  fork test, is-unequal(failed, <>)
    hold
      back leg-failed(failed)
  back leg-ran(run(<java>, make list(<-jar>, jar)), run(<java>, make list(<-jar>, jar, <raise>)))

task rust-leg
  like guard-leg

  fork test, is-equal(find-tool(<cargo>), <>)
    hold
      back leg-skipped(<cargo not installed>)
  save out, compiled(<rust>)
  fork test, not(out/ok)
    hold
      back leg-failed(out/messages/join(< | >))
  save folder, temp-folder(<term-guard-native->)
  save project, guard-path/join(folder, <rust>)
  make-folder(guard-path/join(project, <src>))
  write-file(guard-path/join(project, <Cargo.toml>), cargo-toml)
  write-file(guard-path/join(project, <src>, <main.rs>), <{prelude-text(out, <rust>)}\n{emit-text(out, <rust>)}\n{rust-main}>)
  save target, guard-path/join(guard-os/tmpdir(), <seed-rust-runtime>, <target>)
  save environment, make hash
  save name, <CARGO_TARGET_DIR>
  save environment/{name}, target
  save failed, run-tool(make(list, <cargo>, <build>, <--quiet>), project, environment)
  fork test, is-unequal(failed, <>)
    hold
      back leg-failed(failed)
  save binary, guard-path/join(target, <debug>, <term-guard-native>)
  back leg-ran(run(binary, make list), run(binary, make list(<raise>)))

task leg-made
  take env, like text
  like guard-leg

  save only, variable(<GN_ONLY>)
  fork test, and(is-unequal(only, <>), is-unequal(only, env))
    hold
      back leg-skipped(<GN_ONLY names {only}>)
  fork test, is-equal(env, <swift>)
    hold
      back swift-leg()
  fork test, is-equal(env, <kotlin>)
    hold
      back kotlin-leg()
  back rust-leg()

task leg-held
  take env, like text
  like boolean

  back guard-held/held/has(env)

task leg-at
  take env, like text
  like guard-leg

  back guard-held/held/{env}

task leg-keep
  take env, like text
  take made, like guard-leg
  like void

  save guard-held/held/{env}, made

# the leg of a backend, made once
task leg-of
  take env, like text
  like guard-leg

  fork test, leg-held(env)
    hold
      back leg-at(env)
  save made, leg-made(env)
  leg-keep(env, made)
  back made

# a printed line of a leg that ran, <> past its end
task line-of
  take leg, like guard-leg
  take at, like number
  like text

  fork test, is-below(at, leg/lines/length)
    hold
      back leg/lines/{at}
  back <>

# the uncaught raise's stderr names the exception's form and note
task names-raise
  take leg, like guard-leg
  like boolean

  back and(text-contains(leg/raised-error, <user-absence>), text-contains(leg/raised-error, <No such user>))

# swift

test <swift: the guard program builds>
  host leg, leg-of(<swift>)
  fork test, is-equal(leg/state, <skipped>)
    hold
      skip leg/reason
  want hold, is-equal(leg/state, <ran>)

test <swift: the happy path returns>
  host leg, leg-of(<swift>)
  fork test, is-unequal(leg/state, <ran>)
    hold
      skip <the swift leg did not run: {leg/state}>
  want hold, is-equal(line-of(leg, 0), want-found)

test <swift: the raise reaches the handler with its form and note>
  host leg, leg-of(<swift>)
  fork test, is-unequal(leg/state, <ran>)
    hold
      skip <the swift leg did not run: {leg/state}>
  want hold, is-equal(line-of(leg, 1), want-caught)

test <swift: a fork case over the caught value binds the form's prop>
  host leg, leg-of(<swift>)
  fork test, is-unequal(leg/state, <ran>)
    hold
      skip <the swift leg did not run: {leg/state}>
  want hold, is-equal(line-of(leg, 2), want-cased)

test <swift: an interpolated text raises failure with the text as its note>
  host leg, leg-of(<swift>)
  fork test, is-unequal(leg/state, <ran>)
    hold
      skip <the swift leg did not run: {leg/state}>
  want hold, is-equal(line-of(leg, 3), want-text)

test <swift: an arm that binds the caught time raises another exception>
  host leg, leg-of(<swift>)
  fork test, is-unequal(leg/state, <ran>)
    hold
      skip <the swift leg did not run: {leg/state}>
  want hold, is-equal(line-of(leg, 4), want-translated)

test <swift: an uncaught raise ends the program>
  host leg, leg-of(<swift>)
  fork test, is-unequal(leg/state, <ran>)
    hold
      skip <the swift leg did not run: {leg/state}>
  want hold, is-unequal(leg/raised-code, 0)

test <swift: the uncaught raise names its form and note>
  host leg, leg-of(<swift>)
  fork test, is-unequal(leg/state, <ran>)
    hold
      skip <the swift leg did not run: {leg/state}>
  want hold, names-raise(leg)

# kotlin

test <kotlin: the guard program builds>
  host leg, leg-of(<kotlin>)
  fork test, is-equal(leg/state, <skipped>)
    hold
      skip leg/reason
  want hold, is-equal(leg/state, <ran>)

test <kotlin: the happy path returns>
  host leg, leg-of(<kotlin>)
  fork test, is-unequal(leg/state, <ran>)
    hold
      skip <the kotlin leg did not run: {leg/state}>
  want hold, is-equal(line-of(leg, 0), want-found)

test <kotlin: the raise reaches the handler with its form and note>
  host leg, leg-of(<kotlin>)
  fork test, is-unequal(leg/state, <ran>)
    hold
      skip <the kotlin leg did not run: {leg/state}>
  want hold, is-equal(line-of(leg, 1), want-caught)

test <kotlin: a fork case over the caught value binds the form's prop>
  host leg, leg-of(<kotlin>)
  fork test, is-unequal(leg/state, <ran>)
    hold
      skip <the kotlin leg did not run: {leg/state}>
  want hold, is-equal(line-of(leg, 2), want-cased)

test <kotlin: an interpolated text raises failure with the text as its note>
  host leg, leg-of(<kotlin>)
  fork test, is-unequal(leg/state, <ran>)
    hold
      skip <the kotlin leg did not run: {leg/state}>
  want hold, is-equal(line-of(leg, 3), want-text)

test <kotlin: an arm that binds the caught time raises another exception>
  host leg, leg-of(<kotlin>)
  fork test, is-unequal(leg/state, <ran>)
    hold
      skip <the kotlin leg did not run: {leg/state}>
  want hold, is-equal(line-of(leg, 4), want-translated)

test <kotlin: an uncaught raise ends the program>
  host leg, leg-of(<kotlin>)
  fork test, is-unequal(leg/state, <ran>)
    hold
      skip <the kotlin leg did not run: {leg/state}>
  want hold, is-unequal(leg/raised-code, 0)

test <kotlin: the uncaught raise names its form and note>
  host leg, leg-of(<kotlin>)
  fork test, is-unequal(leg/state, <ran>)
    hold
      skip <the kotlin leg did not run: {leg/state}>
  want hold, names-raise(leg)

# the JVM's own ArithmeticException reached the guard as `failure`, where TypeScript raises `defect`
test <kotlin: a division by a nonzero divisor answers>
  host leg, leg-of(<kotlin>)
  fork test, is-unequal(leg/state, <ran>)
    hold
      skip <the kotlin leg did not run: {leg/state}>
  want hold, is-equal(line-of(leg, 5), <2>)

test <kotlin: a division by zero raises the defect TypeScript raises>
  host leg, leg-of(<kotlin>)
  fork test, is-unequal(leg/state, <ran>)
    hold
      skip <the kotlin leg did not run: {leg/state}>
  want hold, is-equal(line-of(leg, 6), <caught defect>)

test <kotlin: a remainder by zero raises the same defect>
  host leg, leg-of(<kotlin>)
  fork test, is-unequal(leg/state, <ran>)
    hold
      skip <the kotlin leg did not run: {leg/state}>
  want hold, is-equal(line-of(leg, 7), <caught defect>)

# rust

test <rust: the guard program builds>
  host leg, leg-of(<rust>)
  fork test, is-equal(leg/state, <skipped>)
    hold
      skip leg/reason
  want hold, is-equal(leg/state, <ran>)

test <rust: the happy path returns>
  host leg, leg-of(<rust>)
  fork test, is-unequal(leg/state, <ran>)
    hold
      skip <the rust leg did not run: {leg/state}>
  want hold, is-equal(line-of(leg, 0), want-found)

test <rust: the raise reaches the handler with its form and note>
